## engram

```
Self-hosted, correctable, OAuth-secured memory for coding agents

Usage:
  engram [flags]
  engram [command]

Available Commands:
  backfill-short-ids  Assign a short_id to every memory that lacks one (payload-only; no re-embed)
  completion          Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  help                Help about any command
  list                List memories on a remote engram server
  migrate-remap-owner Re-stamp record owner across the collection (sub->email, email->email, owner-less, or anonymous bucket)
  prune-expired       Delete memories whose validity window (not_after) has lapsed
  reindex             Re-embed memories into a new (new-dimension) collection for embedder migration
  search              Search memories on a remote engram server
  serve               Run the engram MCP server
  spine-review        Inventory, verify, and curate the memory spine
  store               Store a memory on a remote engram server
  summarize-missing   Fill empty recall summaries with the configured cheap model
  version             Print the engram version

Flags:
  -h, --help      help for engram
  -v, --version   version for engram

Use "engram [command] --help" for more information about a command.
```

## engram backfill-short-ids

```
Assign a short_id to every memory that lacks one (payload-only; no re-embed)

Usage:
  engram backfill-short-ids [flags]

Flags:
      --dry-run            count records missing a short_id without writing
  -h, --help               help for backfill-short-ids
      --output string      output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --timeout duration   max wall-clock (0 disables); also cancellable via Ctrl-C (default 5m0s)
```

## engram list

```
List memories on a remote engram server

Usage:
  engram list [flags]

Flags:
      --categories strings      category filter (empty = all categories)
      --created-after string    RFC3339 inclusive lower bound on created_at
      --created-before string   RFC3339 exclusive upper bound on created_at
      --cross-spine             span every scope you can read; mutually exclusive with --scope
      --cursor-mode             opt into cursor paging on the first (tokenless) page; cursor_mode, offset, and page_token are mutually exclusive
      --full                    return full content instead of summaries
  -h, --help                    help for list
      --insecure                skip TLS certificate verification (always warns on stderr; no environment fallback)
      --limit uint              max results (0 = server default)
      --offset uint             offset-for-UI paging; cursor_mode, offset, and page_token are mutually exclusive
      --output string           output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --page-token string       opaque cursor from a previous response's next_page_token; cursor_mode, offset, and page_token are mutually exclusive
      --scope string            scope is required unless cross_spine is true; omit and pass --cross-spine to span every scope you can read; mutually exclusive with --cross-spine
      --server string           engram server base URL (default: ENGRAM_SERVER_URL)
      --tags strings            tag filter (records must carry ALL listed tags)
      --timeout string          per-request client deadline (must be > 0, e.g. 30s, 2m; a value of 0 is rejected, never treated as unbounded — unlike this binary's operator-command --timeout, where 0 disables) (default "30s")
      --token-file string       path to a file containing the bearer credential (default: ENGRAM_TOKEN env var)
      --visibility string       visibility filter: "" (all), "private", or "shared"
```

## engram migrate-remap-owner

```
Re-stamp record owner across the collection (sub->email, email->email, owner-less, or anonymous bucket)

Usage:
  engram migrate-remap-owner [flags]

Flags:
      --apply              a destructive operator command previews by default and mutates only when apply is set
      --from string        current owner value to remap (a sub or email); mutually exclusive with --from-missing/--from-anon
      --from-anon          remap the explicit anonymous bucket (owner=="")
      --from-missing       remap owner-less (pre-isolation) records
  -h, --help               help for migrate-remap-owner
      --output string      output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --timeout duration   max wall-clock (must be > 0); also cancellable via Ctrl-C (default 5m0s)
      --to string          new owner value to stamp (required)
```

## engram migrate-set-owner

```
Backfill owner (OIDC sub) onto pre-isolation memory records

Usage:
  engram migrate-set-owner [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help               help for migrate-set-owner
      --output string      output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --owner string       OIDC sub to stamp onto owner-less records (required, non-empty)
      --timeout duration   max wall-clock for the backfill (must be > 0); also cancellable via Ctrl-C (default 5m0s)
```

## engram prune-expired

```
Delete memories whose validity window (not_after) has lapsed

Usage:
  engram prune-expired [flags]

Flags:
      --apply                 a destructive operator command previews by default and mutates only when apply is set
  -h, --help                  help for prune-expired
      --older-than duration   grace period: only prune records whose not_after lapsed at least this long ago (0 = any past not_after)
      --output string         output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --timeout duration      max wall-clock for the sweep (0 disables); also cancellable via Ctrl-C (default 5m0s)
```

## engram reindex

```
Re-embed memories into a new (new-dimension) collection for embedder migration

Usage:
  engram reindex [flags]

Flags:
      --dry-run            scan and count without creating the target or writing
  -h, --help               help for reindex
      --output string      output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --resume             skip points already present in the target with identical content (cheap restart of an interrupted reindex)
      --source string      source collection to read from (default: ENGRAM_QDRANT_COLLECTION)
      --target string      target collection to create and populate (required)
      --timeout duration   max wall-clock for the reindex; 0 means no deadline (Ctrl-C or SIGTERM aborts either way) (default 30m0s)
```

## engram search

```
Search memories on a remote engram server

Usage:
  engram search [flags]

Flags:
      --categories strings      category filter (ANY listed category)
      --created-after string    RFC3339 inclusive lower bound on created_at
      --created-before string   RFC3339 exclusive upper bound on created_at
      --cross-spine             span every scope you can read; mutually exclusive with --scope
      --full                    return full content instead of summaries
  -h, --help                    help for search
      --insecure                skip TLS certificate verification (always warns on stderr; no environment fallback)
      --k uint                  max results (0 = server default)
      --output string           output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --query string            search query (required)
      --scope string            scope is required unless cross_spine is true; mutually exclusive with --cross-spine
      --server string           engram server base URL (default: ENGRAM_SERVER_URL)
      --tags strings            tag filter (records must carry ALL listed tags)
      --timeout string          per-request client deadline (must be > 0, e.g. 30s, 2m; a value of 0 is rejected, never treated as unbounded — unlike this binary's operator-command --timeout, where 0 disables) (default "30s")
      --token-file string       path to a file containing the bearer credential (default: ENGRAM_TOKEN env var)
```

## engram serve

```
Run the engram MCP server

Usage:
  engram serve [flags]

Flags:
      --connect-headless string         mount the ConnectRPC lane on a headless deployment (default off; requires at least one configured auth lane) (default "false")
  -h, --help                            help for serve
      --listen-addr string              listen address (default ":8080")
      --mcp-path string                 path for the MCP transport (empty=/mcp; '/'=legacy root catch-all)
      --oidc-audience string            expected OIDC audience (optional)
      --oidc-client-id string           OIDC confidential-client ID for the web login
      --oidc-client-secret string       OIDC client secret for the web login
      --oidc-issuer string              OIDC issuer URL; setting it enables bearer-token enforcement
      --oidc-resource-metadata string   WWW-Authenticate resource metadata URL (optional)
      --owner-claim string              OIDC claim whose value becomes the record owner / authz key (default email) (default "email")
      --ui-cookie-key string            32-byte AES-GCM key sealing the session cookie
      --ui-enabled string               enable the web UI + login lane (empty=imply from creds; 'false'=hard off)
      --ui-issuer string                OIDC issuer for the web-UI login lane (empty=default to --oidc-issuer)
      --ui-redirect-url string          OIDC auth-code callback URL
```

## engram spine-review

```
Inventory, verify, and curate the memory spine

Usage:
  engram spine-review [command]

Available Commands:
  archive     Archive one or more records by id (reversible via restore)
  consolidate Report ranked near-duplicate candidate pairs across the memory spine
  purge       Delete purge-eligible records, gated on an extraction precondition
  restore     Restore one or more previously-archived records by id
  scan        Report an inventory of the memory spine
  verify      Classify every stored citation as valid, moved, broken, or unverifiable

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for spine-review

Use "engram spine-review [command] --help" for more information about a command.
```

## engram spine-review archive

```
Archive one or more records by id (reversible via restore)

Usage:
  engram spine-review archive [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help               help for archive
      --id strings         id (or short_id) of a record to archive; may be repeated
      --output string      output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --timeout duration   max wall-clock for the run (0 disables); also cancellable via Ctrl-C (default 5m0s)
```

## engram spine-review consolidate

```
Report ranked near-duplicate candidate pairs across the memory spine

Usage:
  engram spine-review consolidate [flags]

Flags:
      --all-scopes         span every scope; a candidate pair may then cross scopes, and each row names both (mutually exclusive with --scope)
  -h, --help               help for consolidate
      --min-score string   minimum cosine score a pair must carry to be reported; absent (the default) means NO filter at all — including pairs with a negative score
      --output string      output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --scope string       only consider records in this scope
      --timeout duration   max wall-clock for the sweep (0 disables); also cancellable via Ctrl-C (default 5m0s)
      --top-k uint         neighbours considered per record (default 5)
```

## engram spine-review purge

```
Delete purge-eligible records under one or more structural classes (superseded, expired, archived) or a free-form filter (category/tags/older-than, which requires an explicit --scope). Every candidate must satisfy rule 7smp8vy9hr's extract-before-delete gate: a server-set superseded_by link to a later record, or an authoritative milestone-summary record covering the batch. a preview cannot be carried into a later invocation: --apply re-derives eligibility within its own run and deletes only the intersection of what it just showed and what is still eligible at that moment. the two derivations run milliseconds apart in one process, so the intersection guards against a concurrent writer changing eligibility in that window, not against operator delay -- the extract gate, the mandatory --scope on the filter path, and the discovery/rule category exclusions carry the real safety weight. the per-record path reads the server-set superseded_by link and cannot be satisfied by anything a caller writes; the batch floor requires a real milestone-summary record whose creation time the server stamped, but its marker tag is caller-mintable, so that path validates a convention, not proof of preservation.

Usage:
  engram spine-review purge [flags]

Flags:
      --all-scopes            span every scope; mutually exclusive with --scope
      --apply                 a destructive operator command previews by default and mutates only when apply is set
      --category string       free-form filter: only this category; the free-form filter path requires an explicit --scope or --all-scopes: category or tags always engage it, and older-than engages it when no class is selected
      --class strings         structural eligibility class (repeatable): superseded, expired, archived
  -h, --help                  help for purge
      --older-than duration   grace/retention window override for the selected class(es) (0 = each class's own default: immediate for superseded/expired, 90 days for archived); with NO class selected, a free-form created-more-than-this-long-ago filter -- the free-form filter path requires an explicit --scope or --all-scopes: category or tags always engage it, and older-than engages it when no class is selected
      --output string         output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --scope string          restrict the derivation to one scope
      --tags strings          free-form filter: records must carry ALL listed tags (repeatable); the free-form filter path requires an explicit --scope or --all-scopes: category or tags always engage it, and older-than engages it when no class is selected
      --timeout duration      max wall-clock for the run (0 disables); also cancellable via Ctrl-C (default 5m0s)
```

## engram spine-review restore

```
Restore one or more previously-archived records by id

Usage:
  engram spine-review restore [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help               help for restore
      --id strings         id (or short_id) of a previously-archived record to restore; may be repeated
      --output string      output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --timeout duration   max wall-clock for the run (0 disables); also cancellable via Ctrl-C (default 5m0s)
```

## engram spine-review scan

```
Report an inventory of the memory spine

Usage:
  engram spine-review scan [flags]

Flags:
      --all-scopes         sweep every scope (required if --scope is omitted)
  -h, --help               help for scan
      --output string      output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --scope string       only scan records in this scope
      --timeout duration   max wall-clock for the sweep (0 disables); also cancellable via Ctrl-C (default 5m0s)
```

## engram spine-review verify

```
Classify every stored citation as valid, moved, broken, or unverifiable

Usage:
  engram spine-review verify [flags]

Flags:
      --all-scopes         sweep every scope (required if --scope is omitted)
      --fail-on string     fail-on accepts broken, moved, unverifiable, or any; omitted, verify exits 0 regardless of findings
  -h, --help               help for verify
      --output string      output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --scope string       only verify citations from records in this scope
      --timeout duration   max wall-clock for the sweep (0 disables); also cancellable via Ctrl-C (default 5m0s)
```

## engram store

```
Store a memory on a remote engram server

Usage:
  engram store [flags]

Flags:
      --base-dir string     base directory
      --category string     category: one of decision, preference, convention, gotcha
      --content string      memory content (required)
  -h, --help                help for store
      --insecure            skip TLS certificate verification (always warns on stderr; no environment fallback)
      --output string       output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --repo string         repo identifier
      --scope string        memory scope (required)
      --server string       engram server base URL (default: ENGRAM_SERVER_URL)
      --source string       source of the memory
      --summary string      client-authored summary
      --tags strings        tags to attach to the memory
      --timeout string      per-request client deadline (must be > 0, e.g. 30s, 2m; a value of 0 is rejected, never treated as unbounded — unlike this binary's operator-command --timeout, where 0 disables) (default "30s")
      --token-file string   path to a file containing the bearer credential (default: ENGRAM_TOKEN env var)
      --workspace string    workspace identifier
      --worktree string     worktree identifier
```

## engram summarize-missing

```
Fill empty recall summaries with the configured cheap model

Usage:
  engram summarize-missing [flags]

Flags:
      --all-scopes            sweep every scope (required if --scope is omitted)
      --dry-run               count eligible records without writing
  -h, --help                  help for summarize-missing
      --limit int             max records to scan (0 = no cap)
      --older-than duration   only records created at least this long ago (0 = any age)
      --output string         output format: "json" or "text" (default: detect from stdout)
      --scope string          only summarize records in this scope
      --timeout duration      max wall-clock for the sweep (0 disables); also cancellable via Ctrl-C (default 30m0s)
```

## engram version

```
Print the engram version

Usage:
  engram version [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for version
```
